<title>USA: Cable &amp; Co Q2 share loss increases.</title>
<headline>Cable &amp; Co Q2 share loss increases.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.85     loss	 $0.03</p>
<p> Net loss		   1,771     loss	    53</p>
<p> Revs			 2,673		    2,011</p>
<p>	  SIX MONTHS ENDED JUNE 30</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $2.39   profit	 $0.02</p>
<p> Net loss		   4,639   profit	    34</p>
<p> Revs			 6,349		    4,715</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE:Full name of company is Cable &amp; Co Worldwide Inc.  </p>
<p>NOTE: The company said $3.268 million of the 1996 Q2 loss was attributable to nonrecurring noncash expenditures relating to the valuation of shares of stock issued to parties associated with the company's initial public offering completed on June 12 1996.</p>
<p>NOTE: An additional $259,000 of the operating loss resulted in nonrecurring items, including accelerated inventory markdowns, among other factors.</p>
